Then we need to allocate dispatch slot for OA and DA. However we have only one dispatch slot DSA. Goal requires both OA and DA linked to same dispatch slot? Actually goal includes candidate_dispatch_slot_linked destination_availability_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha and candidate_dispatch_slot_linked origin_availability_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha. So both need to be linked to same dispatch slot. Is that allowed? The dispatch slot can be linked to multiple candidates? The predicate candidate_dispatch_slot_linked is just a link; there is no constraint that a slot can only be linked to one candidate. However allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate consumes dispatch_slot_available (makes it not available). After allocating for first candidate, dispatch_slot_available becomes false, preventing second allocation. So we cannot allocate same slot to two candidates if we follow that action. However maybe we can allocate slot to OA, then later release? There's no action to release dispatch slot. The only action that makes dispatch_slot_available true is execute_origin_dispatch, execute_destination_dispatch, execute_schedule_dispatch (they release slot after dispatch). So we could allocate slot to OA, then execute origin dispatch (which consumes dispatch_allocated OA and makes slot available again). Then allocate slot to DA, execute destination dispatch. But goal requires both OA and DA to be dispatch_allocated and dispatched? Actually goal includes dispatch_allocated OA, dispatch_allocated DA, dispatch_ready OA, dispatch_ready DA, dispatched OA (but not dispatched DA? Actually goal does not include dispatched DA; only dispatched OA. It also does not require dispatched DA. So we could have OA dispatched, DA not dispatched but still dispatch_allocated and dispatch_ready. However goal includes dispatch_allocated DA and dispatch_ready DA but not dispatched DA. So we need DA to be dispatch_allocated and dispatch_ready but not dispatched. However after we allocate slot to DA and execute destination dispatch, DA would become dispatched and slot available. That would make DA dispatched (not desired). But we could avoid executing destination dispatch; we just need dispatch_allocated DA and dispatch_ready DA, not necessarily dispatched. However goal also includes dispatch_allocated OA and dispatched OA. So we need OA dispatched. So we need to allocate slot to OA, execute origin dispatch (makes OA dispatched and slot available). Then allocate slot to DA (makes DA dispatch_allocated) and mark DA dispatch_ready (we already have). That would satisfy: OA dispatched, OA dispatch_allocated (true after allocate before execute? Actually after allocate, dispatch_allocated OA true; after execute, dispatch_allocated OA becomes false? Wait execute_origin_dispatch effect: (dispatched ?origin_availability) (vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit) (dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot). It does not keep dispatch_allocated true. So after execute, dispatch_allocated OA becomes false. But goal requires dispatch_allocated OA. So we need OA to remain dispatch_allocated after being dispatched? But execute_origin_dispatch removes dispatch_allocated? Actually effect does not include dispatch_allocated; it does not retract it. So dispatch_allocated OA remains true unless there is an explicit negative effect. Since not listed, dispatch_allocated OA stays true. Check: effect: (and (dispatched ?origin_availability) (vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit) (dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot)). No mention of dispatch_allocated. So dispatch_allocated OA persists. Good. So after execute, OA still dispatch_allocated. So we can allocate slot to OA, execute origin dispatch, OA becomes dispatched, slot becomes available again, OA still dispatch_allocated. Then allocate slot to DA (makes DA dispatch_allocated) and we keep DA dispatch_ready (we already have). No need to execute destination dispatch. So final state: OA dispatched, OA dispatch_allocated, OA dispatch_ready (still true after mark? Does execute affect dispatch_ready? No. So OA dispatch_ready remains true unless some action unsets it (none). So OA dispatch_ready stays true. DA dispatch_allocated true (after allocate), DA dispatch_ready true (from earlier mark). DA not dispatched (since we didn't execute). Good.

Now we also need vehicle_available VUA. After execute_origin_dispatch, vehicle_available VUA becomes true. Initially VUA allocated to OA; after execute, VUA becomes available. Good.

Now we need compliance_certificate_available CCA. Initially CCA is linked to SCA (shift_candidate_alpha) via candidate_compliance_certificate_linked. So CCA is not available. We need to release it via release_compliance_certificate action: parameters ?candidate - schedule_candidate ?compliance_certificate - compliance_certificate. Precondition: candidate_compliance_certificate_linked ?candidate ?compliance_certificate. Effect: compliance_certificate_available ?compliance_certificate, not candidate_compliance_certificate_linked ?candidate ?compliance_certificate. So we need to release CCA from SCA. SCA is a schedule_candidate (shift_candidate_alpha). So we can do release_compliance_certificate shift_candidate_alpha CCA.

Now we need to ensure that after releasing, CCA becomes available. Also note that SCA currently has many other links (candidate_destination_availability_linked, candidate_origin_availability_linked, candidate_transport_leg_linked, candidate_vehicle_linked, candidate_loading_container_linked, candidate_dispatch_slot_linked, candidate_finalized, candidate_prepared, etc). Releasing compliance certificate just removes that link; fine.

Now we need to check if any other goal conditions require something else: we also need transport_leg_origin_linked and destination_linked (we will have from assemble). transport_leg_loading_authorized (we will have). transport_leg_assembled true.

Now we need to ensure we haven't inadvertently broken any preconditions due to other actions.

Let's outline plan steps in order:

1. detach_task_profile destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha
   (makes RTPA available)

2. attach_task_profile origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha
   (links OA to RTPA)

3. confirm_candidate_preparedness origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha
   (makes OA prepared)

4. assign_operator_resource origin_availability_alpha driver_operator_alpha
   (links OA to operator)

5. activate_origin_node origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha
   (makes origin_node_ready)

6. load_origin_payload origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha cargo_payload_alpha
   (sets origin_node_occupied, origin_availability_locked, origin_payload_linked, cargo not available)

7. unload_origin_payload origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha cargo_payload_alpha
   (sets origin_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed, cargo_available, keeps origin_node_occupied and origin_availability_locked)

Now OA: prepared, operator linked, node ready, node occupied, availability locked and confirmed, cargo available.

